      <p>5. Faculty Advisor</p>
      <ol class="list-[lower-alpha] pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>A faculty member of the Nuclear Engineering Program shall volunteer for the position.</li>
        <li>The Faculty Advisor must be a Fellow, Member, or Emeritus member of the American Nuclear Society and a faculty member in the Nuclear Engineering Program at The Ohio State University.</li>
        <li>The Faculty Advisor shall serve as a non-voting member of the Section, except in matters pertaining to the voluntary dissolution of the organization, wherein the advisor shall retain voting privileges.</li>
        <li>The tenure of the Faculty Advisor shall remain in effect until such time as the Academic Advisor formally submits a request for removal from the position, or until a unanimous resolution is passed by the Board of Governors during a duly convened public meeting. The said meeting shall be specifically convened to consider the appointment or replacement of the current Faculty Advisor.</li>
        <li>Replacement mechanisms are:
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-1">
