        <li>Proposal: Amendments to these Rules may be proposed at any Board meeting or during any regular Section meeting.</li>
        <li>Comment Period: The Board shall allow a two (2)-week comment period before voting on proposed amendments.</li>
        <li>Board Endorsement: Upon endorsement by at least two-thirds (2/3) of the Board of Governors, proposed Rules shall be submitted to the Society Bylaws and Rules Committee for review.</li>
        <li>Society Review: The Committee shall provide comments for improving consistency and clarity in accordance with the intent of proposed amendments.</li>
        <li>Final Vote: Once comments are resolved and endorsed by the Committee, the Board shall vote on proposed amendments, with a simple majority of quorum being sufficient for passage.</li>
        <li>Membership Ratification: Any Board member may request presentation of proposed amendments to Section membership. A simple majority of not less than twenty-five percent (25%) of total voting membership shall be sufficient for passage.</li>
        <li>Implementation: Approved amendments become effective upon the Secretary's filing of amended Rules with Society Headquarters.</li>
        <li>Notification: The Secretary shall notify members of amendments as soon as possible after adoption via accessible media.</li>
      </ol>
    `,
  },
  {
    id: "b12",
    title: "B12/R12 — Dissolution",
    bylaws: `<p>1. Upon the dissolution of the Section, assets shall be distributed first in accordance with the Articles of Incorporation of the Section. If no such Articles exist, or potential recipients are not named specifically, then the Society, an organization exempt under Section 501(c)(3) of the Internal Revenue Code, shall take possession of assets for one or more exempt purposes within the meaning of that Section of the Code or corresponding section of any future federal tax code, or they shall be distributed to the Federal government, or to a state or local government, for a public purpose.</p>`,
    rules: `
      <p>1. Dissolution Requirements</p>
      <ol class="list-[lower-alpha] pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Voluntary dissolution requires approval by:
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-1">
            <li>Four out of five Board of Governors members (Core Officers plus Executive Officers)</li>
            <li>Three-fourths of the general membership</li>
            <li>Faculty Advisor</li>
          </ol>
        </li>
        <li>Debt Restriction: The Section cannot be dissolved while maintaining active debts with banks, vendors, contractors, or other creditors.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>2. Financial Clearance Process — Before dissolution proceedings may commence:</p>
      <ol class="list-[lower-alpha] pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Treasurer must prepare a comprehensive financial report detailing the complete financial status, including all assets, liabilities, outstanding debts, pending transactions, and financial obligations</li>
        <li>If debts exist, the Treasurer must work to resolve all outstanding financial obligations</li>
        <li>Board must review and accept the financial report confirming debt resolution before the dissolution vote</li>
      </ol>
      <p>3. Asset Distribution — Upon approved dissolution:</p>
      <ol class="list-[lower-alpha] pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Assets distributed per Articles of Incorporation or to Society as a 501(c)(3) organization</li>
        <li>Financial holdings, records, and materials may be distributed to an approved interim storage facility or the National American Nuclear Society per applicable regulations</li>
      </ol>
      <p>4. Documentation Requirements — All dissolution proceedings must be fully documented and filed with the appropriate University and Society authorities in accordance with applicable regulations.</p>
    `,
  },
];
---

<div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
  <div class="px-6 py-5 border-b border-gray-200">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Bylaws and Rules</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">
      Revised October 11, 2025 &middot; Approved by the Board October 13, 2025
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-600 mt-3">
      The Standard Bylaws (derived from the national ANS Bylaws and Rules, and
      only amendable by the Society's Board of Governors) are shown alongside
      the Section's own Rules, which this chapter develops and maintains. If
      the two conflict, the Bylaws take precedence.
    </p>
  </div>

  <nav aria-label="Bylaws and Rules sections" class="px-6 py-4 border-b border-gray-200 bg-gray-50">
    <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm">
      {sections.map((s) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`#${s.id}`} class="text-primary-600 hover:underline">{s.title}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <div class="divide-y divide-gray-200">
    {sections.map((s) => (
      <section id={s.id} class="px-6 py-8 scroll-mt-24">
        <h4 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">{s.title}</h4>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 mb-2">
              Standard Bylaws
            </p>
            <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-3" set:html={s.bylaws} />
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 mb-2">
              OSU Section Rules
            </p>
            <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-3" set:html={s.rules} />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>
</div>
